Vendored runtime, compositor input and clipboard sources, KRFB patches, and GPU
compatibility sources. Existing source copyright and license notices are retained.
The test-only RFB client in ../../tests/rfb.py is copied from the same source commit.

Local changes:
- X11 kiosk sessions require kwin_x11, without requiring startplasma-x11.
- Kiosk Qt clients use the generic theme, avoiding Qt 6.11's built-in KDE theme
  startup crash when the optional Plasma integration package is absent.
- Restart the compositor after successful exits too: KWin's wrapper returns zero
  when it exhausts its crash retries. Explicit systemd stops still stop it.
- Debian and Ubuntu source variants use the isolated /opt/kwin-6.8.2 stack. Its
  Qt/KF paths and service cache are scoped to KWin and its matching KScreen
  output client; distro applications retain their original library/plugin
  environment. KWin 6.8 changed the output-device registry protocol.
- Allocate and initialize KRFB's virtual-monitor framebuffer before publishing
  its dimensions. An early VNC pixel request otherwise dereferences null before
  PipeWire delivers the first captured frame.
- Debian KWin 6.3 NVIDIA VNC/web sessions use the software-capture workaround
  only when the optional /opt/kwin-6.8.2 compositor is absent. Source KWin 6.8.2
  retains the normal GPU path in every mode.
- Arch builds the separately namespaced upstream KWin X11 release because its
  current repositories no longer publish kwin-x11.
- Forced Wayland nesting also mounts the host X11 socket when clipboard sync is
  enabled, allowing the Weston clipboard bridge to use its Xwayland fallback.
- The test-only GUI fixture can capture actual headless outputs through KWin's
  ScreenShot2 API or the X11 root screen. Its Save button has a solid color so
  input tests can locate and click the rendered control across nested displays.
